{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":64,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivity_and_order_five_give_chi_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivity_and_order_five_give_chi_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":491,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L491-L496","doc":"The two inputs together give `χ = −6` — stated so the dependence is explicit:\nit is a consequence of *transitivity + order 5*, not of the five axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.order_five_selects_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.order_five_selects_bring","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L486-L489","doc":"**An order-5 automorphism selects Bring.**  By Cauchy, order 5 occurs iff\n`5 ∣ |Aut|`; only the genus-4 case qualifies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.classificationAutOrders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.classificationAutOrders","kind":"def","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L482-L484","doc":"Automorphism-group orders of the three curves in the classification:\nBring `|S₅| = 120`, Klein `|PSL(2,7)| = 168`, and the genus-3 `|S₄| = 24`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivity_narrows_chi_to_two_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivity_narrows_chi_to_two_values","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L477-L480","doc":"**Homogeneity narrows `χ(A)` to two values.**  Contrast §1, where the derived\nsteps leave every non-positive even integer open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivityAdmissibleGenera","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.transitivityAdmissibleGenera","kind":"def","line":474,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L474-L475","doc":"The genera admitted by the Laing–Singerman transitivity classification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow_and_orbit_readings_disagree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow_and_orbit_readings_disagree","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L436-L444","doc":"**The two readings of \"6\" disagree, in both directions.**  This is the\nstatement that kills the ADE route even after finiteness and the icosahedral type\nare granted: the integer 6 is a property of the chosen invariant, not of the\ngroup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5CountA5_is_a_sylow_candidate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5CountA5_is_a_sylow_candidate","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L434-L434","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5CountA5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5CountA5","kind":"def","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L429-L432","doc":"`n₅(A₅) = 6`: the larger of the two Sylow candidates, since `A₅` is simple\nand a normal Sylow-5 would contradict that.  The simplicity input is cited\n(`[klein1888]` for the icosahedral group; standard for `A₅`), not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_is_not_a_sylow3_count_for_A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_is_not_a_sylow3_count_for_A4","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L427-L427","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow3_candidates_A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow3_candidates_A4","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L422-L425","doc":"**Sylow-3 in `A₄`** (the tetrahedral rotation group): `|A₄|/3 = 4`, so\n`n₃ ∈ {1, 4}` — and **6 is not among them**, whichever way the ambiguity is\nresolved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5_candidates_A5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylow5_candidates_A5","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L419-L420","doc":"**Sylow-5 in `A₅`**: `|A₅|/5 = 12`, so `n₅ ∈ {1, 6}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylowCandidates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.sylowCandidates","kind":"def","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L413-L417","doc":"Candidates for `n_p` allowed by Sylow's theorems: divisors `n` of `|G|/p`\nwith `n % p = 1`.  Decidable, and computed rather than asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.observability_leaves_four_families_that_disagree_about_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.observability_leaves_four_families_that_disagree_about_six","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L383-L394","doc":"**Observability prunes one family and leaves four.**  Stated together with\nthe orbit facts so that the conjunction is not a restatement of a single table:\nthe family the axiom keeps and the family an orbit-reading of `6` selects are\ndifferent families. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.adjointInvariantDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.adjointInvariantDim","kind":"def","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L373-L381","doc":"`dim (Ad)^Ḡ` — the dimension of the fixed subspace of the 3-dimensional\nadjoint (rotation) representation.  A cyclic rotation group fixes its axis, so 1;\nevery other finite rotation group fixes no line, so 0.  Classical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.icosahedral_orbits_at_least_twelve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.icosahedral_orbits_at_least_twelve","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L349-L352","doc":"The icosahedral orbit sizes are all at least 12, so no reading that produces\na number below 12 can be an icosahedral orbit count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_orbit_excludes_icosahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_orbit_excludes_icosahedral","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L340-L347","doc":"**The negative this bean was opened to test.**  Reading the branch-point\ncount as the size of an exceptional orbit of the ADE group on `ℙ(V)` excludes the\nicosahedral case and admits the tetrahedral, octahedral and dihedral-6 cases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.klein_constraint_dihedral_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.klein_constraint_dihedral_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L333-L336","doc":"…and for the dihedral and cyclic families at sample parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.klein_constraint_exceptional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.klein_constraint_exceptional","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L325-L331","doc":"**Klein's relation holds for the three exceptional families**, which\ncross-checks every cone order and orbit size in `coneOrders` /\n`exceptionalOrbitSizes` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.kleinDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.kleinDefect","kind":"def","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L321-L323","doc":"Left-hand side of Klein's relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_icosahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_icosahedral","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L308-L308","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_octahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_octahedral","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L307-L307","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_tetrahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.orbits_tetrahedral","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L306-L306","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.exceptionalOrbitSizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.exceptionalOrbitSizes","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L301-L304","doc":"Sizes of the exceptional orbits on `ℙ(V)`: the orbit over the cone point of\norder `m` has size `|Ḡ| / m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.coneOrders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.coneOrders","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L292-L299","doc":"Cone orders of the quotient orbifold `ℙ(V)/Ḡ`: `S²(n,n)`, `S²(2,2,n)`,\n`S²(2,3,3)`, `S²(2,3,4)`, `S²(2,3,5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.rotationOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.rotationOrder","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L283-L290","doc":"Order of the **rotation** group in `SO(3)`; the binary group in `SU(2)` has\ntwice this order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instReprADEType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instReprADEType.repr","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L281-L281","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instReprADEType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instReprADEType","kind":"instance","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L281-L281","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instDecidableEqADEType.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instDecidableEqADEType.decEq","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L281-L281","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instDecidableEqADEType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.instDecidableEqADEType","kind":"instance","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L281-L281","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.icosahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.icosahedral","kind":"ctor","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L280-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.octahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.octahedral","kind":"ctor","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L279-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.tetrahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.tetrahedral","kind":"ctor","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L278-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.dihedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.dihedral","kind":"ctor","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L277-L277","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType.cyclic","kind":"ctor","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L276-L276","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ADEType","kind":"inductive","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L271-L281","doc":"The five families of finite subgroups of `SU(2)` (McKay's ADE list), named by\nthe rotation group they cover in `SO(3) = SU(2)/{±1}`.  `cyclic n` and\n`dihedral n` carry the rotation group's parameter; `dihedral n` is intended for\n`n ≥ 2` (`dihedral 1` is cyclic of order 2 and is not a separate family). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_pair_is_the_generic_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_pair_is_the_generic_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L229-L231","doc":"The corpus's `(T₂,₉, T₂,₁₁)` is exactly the generic bracketing pair at\n`g = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.torus_knot_pair_brackets_every_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.torus_knot_pair_brackets_every_genus","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L222-L227","doc":"**Every genus has a bracketing pair.**  `T₂,₂g₊₁` embeds on `Σ_g` and\n`T₂,₂g₊₃` does not, for every `g`.  So the shape \"one torus knot embeds, the\nnext does not\" cannot single out `g = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo_eleven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo_eleven","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L220-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo_nine","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.seifertRankTwo","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L216-L217","doc":"Seifert rank of the `(2, s)` torus knot, `(2−1)(s−1)/2 = (s−1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramification_six_not_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramification_six_not_forced","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L195-L199","doc":"**`R = 6` is not forced by `χ = −6` together with `h ≥ 1`.**  Three\n`(degree, base genus, ramification)` triples give `−6`, with ramification 6, 2\nand 0.  The 6 arrives with the choice of base genus, not from `χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chi_over_torus_is_minus_ramification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chi_over_torus_is_minus_ramification","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L187-L193","doc":"**Over a genus-1 base the degree drops out entirely**: `χ = −R` for every\ndegree.  So the repaired reading fixes the ramification at 6 and says nothing\nwhatever about the degree — a second place where the chain's arithmetic is\nweaker than it looks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_quotient_by_transposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_quotient_by_transposition","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L182-L185","doc":"**The repaired Step 5.**  A degree-2 quotient of Bring's curve by a\ntransposition has six fixed points, each contributing `d − 1 = 1`, so `R = 6`;\nthe quotient has genus 1 and `χ(B) = 2·0 − 6 = −6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOfCover_zero_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOfCover_zero_base","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L179-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOfCover","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOfCover","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L175-L177","doc":"`χ` of a degree-`d` cover of a genus-`h` base with total ramification `R`:\n`χ = d·(2 − 2h) − R`.  Generalises `chiOverP1` (`h = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.weierstrass_split_six_by_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.weierstrass_split_six_by_ten","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L170-L173","doc":"**`60 = 6 × 10`** — six Weierstrass points fixed by each of the ten\ntranspositions (`[braden-disney-hogg-2022]`, after Prop. 3.3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.s5TranspositionCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.s5TranspositionCount","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L167-L168","doc":"Transpositions in `S₅`: `C(5,2) = 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_weierstrass_count_ne_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_weierstrass_count_ne_six","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_weierstrass_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.bring_weierstrass_count","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L162-L163","doc":"**Bring's curve has 60 Weierstrass points, not 6.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.weierstrassWeightTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.weierstrassWeightTotal","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L157-L160","doc":"Total Weierstrass weight of a genus-`g` curve, `g³ − g`; equal to the number\nof Weierstrass points exactly when every point has weight 1, which holds for\nBring's curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramification_range_degree_four_six_points","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramification_range_degree_four_six_points","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L133-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramificationHi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramificationHi","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramificationLo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.ramificationLo","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L129-L130","doc":"The ramification range a branch-point count allows: `b ≤ R ≤ b·(d−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_branch_points_degree_four_spans_genus_zero_to_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.six_branch_points_degree_four_spans_genus_zero_to_six","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L119-L127","doc":"**`b = 6` at degree 4 is compatible with every genus from 0 to 6.**  The\nlower end is every branch point simple (`R = b = 6`), the upper end is every\nbranch point totally ramified (`R = b(d−1) = 18`).  So the branch-point count,\ntaken alone with the degree, determines nothing near `g = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_degree_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_degree_three","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L114-L117","doc":"The corpus's degree-3 reading gives the same `χ` with a different `R`\n(`R = 2g − 2 + 2d = 12`), which is why the two blocks are not numerically\ninconsistent even though they describe different maps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_degree_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.corpus_degree_four","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L111-L112","doc":"The corpus's degree-4 reading: `R = 14` is what gives `−6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOverP1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.chiOverP1","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L105-L109","doc":"`χ` of the total space of a degree-`d` branched cover of `ℙ¹` with total\nramification `R`: Riemann–Hurwitz, `χ = d · χ(ℙ¹) − R = 2d − R`.  This is a\n*definition* encoding Riemann–Hurwitz's statement; Mathlib has no\nbranched-covering API and nothing here proves the theorem itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.step34_admissible_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.step34_admissible_iff","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**…and nothing else is.**  The admissible set is exactly the non-positive\neven integers, so the derived steps are neither weaker nor stronger than that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.all_even_nonpos_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.all_even_nonpos_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L74-L77","doc":"**Steps 3 + 4 leave infinitely many values open.**  Every non-positive even\ninteger `−2n` is admissible, realised at genus `n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_eight_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_eight_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_four_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_four_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**The falsifiable half.**  `−4` is admissible for exactly the same reasons\n`−6` is, so Steps 3 + 4 do not distinguish them.  If this failed, Steps 3 + 4\nwould already carry more than they are credited with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_six_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.neg_six_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.Step34Admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.Step34Admissible","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The predicate Steps 3 + 4 of the chain impose on `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.BranchPointSixNotForced.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BranchPointSixNotForced.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Euler characteristic of a closed orientable genus-`g` surface. ","signatureChunk":0}]}